WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.601
-House Republicans voted
to remove

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:05.638
Wyoming Congresswoman Liz Cheney
from a leadership position today

00:00:05.638 --> 00:00:07.306
for the crime of not showing

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:09.142
sufficient loyalty
to Donald Trump.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:11.978
For more on this,
it's time for A Closer Look.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.984
Liz Cheney is among the very
last people in the world

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:19.318
I want to side with,
for one thing,

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:20.753
I doubt we have much in common.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.855
I've never been to Wyoming
and I have no plans to go there,

00:00:22.855 --> 00:00:25.524
not because it isn't beautiful,
which I'm sure it is.

00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:26.893
But as a New Yorker,

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:29.161
if there isn't a bodega
within a five-minute

00:00:29.161 --> 00:00:32.098
walking distance where I can get
batteries, deodorant,

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:35.402
a single roll of toilet paper,
and egg and cheese on a roll,

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:37.003
and hear people complain
about de Blasio

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.505
in multiple languages,
I can't live there.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.707
I can't sleep unless
my upstairs neighbor

00:00:41.707 --> 00:00:44.977
is practicing the flugelhorn
and someone outside is yelling,

00:00:44.977 --> 00:00:50.216
"Christy says
she's going to meet us there!"

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.652
Christy!

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:53.919
More importantly,

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:55.688
Cheney helped
lay the groundwork for Trumpism

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:57.656
in the authoritarian
Republican Party

00:00:57.656 --> 00:01:00.126
that exists today,
she defended illegal torture

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:02.128
and lied about it,
championed the Iraq war,

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.597
and one TV interview
pointedly refused

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.932
to denounce
the racist lie that

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.067
President Obama wasn't
a United States citizen,

00:01:08.067 --> 00:01:09.735
a lie, of course,
that was central

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.337
to Donald Trump's
political rise.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.205
-One of the reasons
I think you see people

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:14.540
so concerned about this,

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:18.044
I think that this issue
is people are uncomfortable

00:01:18.044 --> 00:01:20.146
with having
for the first time ever,

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:23.049
I think, a president
who seems so reluctant

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.185
to defend the nation overseas.

00:01:25.185 --> 00:01:27.553
We've seen this again
and again and again

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.689
where this president
seems to sort of want to --

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.825
-What does that have to --
are you saying that --

00:01:31.825 --> 00:01:33.992
are you saying because
he's a Kenyan?

00:01:33.992 --> 00:01:35.428
-No, I'm not saying that.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.863
I'm saying that people
are fundamentally uncomfortable

00:01:37.863 --> 00:01:39.465
and they're fundamentally,
I think,

00:01:39.465 --> 00:01:42.468
increasingly uncomfortable
with an American president

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:45.471
who seems to be afraid
to defend America.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.807
-Yeah, sure. Obama was afraid
to defend America.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:50.009
The guy you supported
in 2016 bragged

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.544
about exchanging
beautiful letters

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.945
and falling in love
with Kim Jong Un

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:55.581
and got a soccer ball
as a gift from Vladimir Putin

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:57.783
like an 8-year-old
in his first Christmas

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:58.851
with this new stepdad.

00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:00.086
Wow, check it out, Mom.

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:04.623
Soccer balls,
this is way better than Xbox.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:06.625
And sure, Cheney later
issued a statement

00:02:06.625 --> 00:02:09.095
saying she had no questions
about Obama's birth certificate,

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.630
but you don't get
to have it both ways.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:13.333
You don't get to go on TV
and defend birthers

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:16.035
and quietly issue
a mealy mouthed statement

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.069
condemning birthers.

00:02:17.069 --> 00:02:18.138
We all know what you're doing.

00:02:18.138 --> 00:02:20.005
It's like when
I'm at a dinner party

00:02:20.005 --> 00:02:22.108
bragging about how much
I got laid in college.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.576
And then later
on the drive home,

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.211
I tell my wife
I was just kidding,

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.646
that I was a virgin
until we met.

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:29.315
That's why I'm so bad at sex.
Remember?

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.418
Then she very sweetly says,
I do remember.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.286
Cheney even stood by Trump
in 2016

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:35.454
after the "Access Hollywood"
tape,

00:02:35.454 --> 00:02:37.056
with the Associated Press

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.991
reporting that Cheney said,
"Trump's comments are appalling.

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.593
"But Hillary Clinton's actions
are far worse.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:43.529
"Cheney says Clinton's handling
of emails as secretary of state

00:02:43.529 --> 00:02:46.399
put her self-interest
above national security."

00:02:46.399 --> 00:02:48.801
I don't know,
for my money, bus pervert

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.669
is worse than
lax email security.

00:02:50.669 --> 00:02:56.442
But worst of all is a bus
pervert with lax email security.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:57.910
Hey, can I, uh,
take your picture

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.412
for my private photo
collection?

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:02.214
No one's ever going to see this.
It's password protected.

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:06.385
And the password is one,
two, three, four, five!

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:08.821
Everyone get that?

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:11.523
So Cheney cheered on illegal
torture and disastrous war,

00:03:11.523 --> 00:03:12.992
has helped pave
the way for Trump

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:15.928
and stood by him
throughout the 2016 election

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:17.963
and his first impeachment,

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:19.331
but she's not being punished
for any of that.

00:03:19.331 --> 00:03:21.701
She's being punished
for acknowledging the reality

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.336
that Trump lost in 2020

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:25.738
and that there was
no widespread fraud

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.874
and for criticizing him
for inciting

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:29.742
a violent insurrection
to overturn the results.

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.277
Living in reality
should be the bare minimum

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:32.411
for holding public office.

00:03:32.411 --> 00:03:34.814
And yet, today's
GOP is so bat [bleep] crazy,

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.383
simply living in reality
is considered heresy.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.486
Which is why today House
Republicans voted to remove

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:42.655
Cheney from her
leadership position

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:45.524
because she had the temerity
to admit that Trump lost.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:48.428
-House Republicans pushed out
Congresswoman Liz Cheney

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.597
as the number three ranked
member of GOP leadership,

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.065
according to a member
in the room

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:54.567
as the vote happened.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.970
Cheney was booed when she
criticized the former president

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.472
in her opening remarks.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:01.073
-Just like that, it's over.

00:04:01.073 --> 00:04:03.909
The House Republican conference
had a voice vote

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:07.613
that means no recorded total
and has ousted Liz Cheney

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:10.650
from her number three position
within the conference.

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:14.320
-I am absolutely committed,
as I said last night

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.856
and as I said just now
to my colleagues,

00:04:17.856 --> 00:04:21.660
that we must go forward
based on truth.

00:04:21.660 --> 00:04:24.397
We cannot both embrace
the big lie

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:26.065
and embrace the Constitution.

00:04:26.065 --> 00:04:31.070
I will do everything
I can to ensure

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.473
that the former president
never again

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.408
gets anywhere
near the Oval Office.

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:37.042
-All right. First of all,
I don't think you need to worry

00:04:37.042 --> 00:04:39.145
about Trump getting anywhere
near the Oval Office again,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.980
even if he avoids
criminal prosecution,

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.782
runs again in 2024 and wins.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.717
I doubt he'd ever
even leave Mar-a-Lago.

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.486
He seems to be enjoying
his new life there

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:49.088
as the world's worst
wedding deejay.

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:51.958
"The couple has requested
'Midnight Train to Georgia.'

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.459
"And based on the election,

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.861
"I'll tell you what was on
that midnight train, folks.

00:04:55.861 --> 00:04:58.163
"Fraudulent ballots,
especially for Joe because

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.698
"at 11, 11:30,
I'm winning Georgia

00:04:59.698 --> 00:05:01.200
"and then the clock
strikes midnight,

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:03.136
"toot toot,
here comes the fraud train.

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.904
Now I'm losing."

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:07.640
With all that, again,
a second wedding reference

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:11.877
where I showed restraint
and did not do Vince Vaughn.

00:05:11.877 --> 00:05:13.346
The meetings are working.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.681
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:17.817
Vince-a-holic Vanonymous.

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.521
With all that...[ laughs ]

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:25.891
With all that said,
it's truly unnerving

00:05:25.891 --> 00:05:28.460
that the only person
in GOP leadership

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.996
who will suffer any consequences
from the Big Lie

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:34.400
and the January 6 insurrection
that resulted from it

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.570
is the one person who was
willing to speak out against it.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.004
The ringleaders
of the insurrection,

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:40.773
the Ted Cruzes
and Paul Gosars

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:43.809
and Josh Hawleys of the world
are walking away scot free.

00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:45.845
Even Mitt Romney
was apparently so furious

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.546
at Hawley
on the day of the insurrection.

00:05:47.546 --> 00:05:50.516
He screamed at Hawley,
"You have caused this."

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.317
Now, I know there's
one school of thought

00:05:52.317 --> 00:05:53.785
that you have to be
a real [bleep] heel

00:05:53.785 --> 00:05:56.088
to get someone as calm
as Mitt Romney to yell at you.

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.257
But I'm also willing
to bet that off-camera,

00:05:58.257 --> 00:06:00.225
my man Mitt does
a lot of yelling.

00:06:00.225 --> 00:06:02.595
And I bet he's strong, too,
like, real strong.

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:04.397
And I bet if you and your crew
and neighborhood toughs

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.265
surrounded him on the bus
and says stuff like,

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:09.235
"What's the matter, milk breath?
You don't like how loud we are?"

00:06:09.235 --> 00:06:11.771
I bet he would say, "No,
I don't want trouble, boys."

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:14.006
But I bet the next time a bus
goes through that dark tunnel,

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:16.775
all you hear punches
and grunts when it emerges,

00:06:16.775 --> 00:06:18.176
it's just five kids in a pile.

00:06:18.176 --> 00:06:20.946
And I bet it's just Mitt Romney
repomading his hair.

00:06:20.946 --> 00:06:22.548
And when he gets off
at his stop,

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:25.918
he says to the driver,
"I was never here."

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:30.089
That's what I bet.

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:31.723
Call your bookie.

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:34.460
Anyway, only Liz Cheney
will face consequences

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:36.295
simply for living in reality
and criticizing

00:06:36.295 --> 00:06:38.197
Trump's big lie
that the election was stolen,

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.099
which I have to say
is a little surprising

00:06:40.099 --> 00:06:41.667
coming from a party
that claims to believe

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.202
so passionately
in free expression.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:46.138
In fact, in his a statement
announcing today's vote,

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:49.408
GOP House leader Kevin McCarthy
said in one paragraph,

00:06:49.408 --> 00:06:51.844
"These internal conflicts
need to be resolved.

00:06:51.844 --> 00:06:53.645
It's clear that we need
to make a change."

00:06:53.645 --> 00:06:56.716
And then in the next paragraph,
"Unlike the left,

00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.418
we embrace free
thought and debate."

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:02.788
You guys are the ones purging
someone from GOP leadership

00:07:02.788 --> 00:07:04.390
for questioning party dogma.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.458
You like Dorothy at the end of
"The Wizard of Oz."

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:09.094
It turns out the cancer culture
you were looking for

00:07:09.094 --> 00:07:11.530
was right there
inside you all along.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.965
So as we saw from today's vote,

00:07:12.965 --> 00:07:15.501
the party is fully committed
to Donald Trump as its leader.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:18.203
It has no core beliefs,
no core ideology

00:07:18.203 --> 00:07:20.606
other than the big lie
that the election was stolen

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.874
and that any wins by Democrats
are illegitimate.

00:07:22.874 --> 00:07:25.645
That's why Republicans
in a dozen states have already

00:07:25.645 --> 00:07:28.948
implemented draconian voter
suppression laws, with Arizona

00:07:28.948 --> 00:07:30.549
joining them just yesterday.

00:07:30.549 --> 00:07:33.052
And at least 404
voting restriction bills

00:07:33.052 --> 00:07:35.922
have now been introduced in
48 state legislatures,

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.990
including laws
that would limit mail,

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.525
early in-person,
and Election Day voting

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:42.327
with such constraints
as stricter ID requirements,

00:07:42.327 --> 00:07:45.731
limited hours, or narrower
eligibility to vote absentee.

00:07:45.731 --> 00:07:48.234
If Republicans had their way,
voting would be as difficult

00:07:48.234 --> 00:07:50.736
and confusing
as parking in midtown Manhattan.

00:07:50.736 --> 00:07:53.506
No parking except for alternate
Wednesdays and months

00:07:53.506 --> 00:07:55.107
ending in Z
between the hours of

00:07:55.107 --> 00:07:56.775
4 and 5 a.m. during leap years.

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:58.945
Please note this sign
was written on opposite day.

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:00.412
Psych!

00:08:00.412 --> 00:08:02.248
Spent a lot of time

00:08:02.248 --> 00:08:05.584
deciding how to spell psych
on that sign.

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:09.020
And we would just ask you
all to check in

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:13.992
with our very popular digital
exclusive corrections,

00:08:13.992 --> 00:08:15.427
which is available online

00:08:15.427 --> 00:08:19.398
and is a huge, huge hit.

00:08:19.398 --> 00:08:20.633
That's what they're going to air

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.602
instead of the Golden Globes
next year.

00:08:25.304 --> 00:08:28.274
And that's because
the GOP has calculated

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:31.210
that it simply cannot move on
from Donald Trump,

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:33.779
that no matter how unpopular
and destructive

00:08:33.779 --> 00:08:35.881
he is for the country,
they can't succeed

00:08:35.881 --> 00:08:37.283
as a party without him.

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:38.617
Lindsey Graham was even

00:08:38.617 --> 00:08:41.420
surprisingly honest about this
on Fox News last week.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:43.855
-I would just say
to my Republican colleagues,

00:08:43.855 --> 00:08:47.393
can we move forward
without President Trump?

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.661
The answer is no.

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:50.328
I've always liked Liz Cheney,

00:08:50.328 --> 00:08:53.832
but she's made a determination
that the Republican Party

00:08:53.832 --> 00:08:56.969
can't grow with
President Trump.

00:08:56.969 --> 00:08:59.304
I've determined we can't
grow without him.

00:08:59.304 --> 00:09:02.174
If you don't get that
as a Republican,

00:09:02.174 --> 00:09:03.575
you're making
the biggest mistake

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:05.410
in the history
of the Republican Party.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:08.180
The reason our party
is growing with minorities

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:11.183
and with working men and women
is because President Trump

00:09:11.183 --> 00:09:15.621
appears to be on the side
of people working really hard.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:18.323
-He's on the side of
people working really hard.

00:09:18.323 --> 00:09:20.159
Yeah, I work really hard
every weekend

00:09:20.159 --> 00:09:23.729
at my meemaw's antique store,
and she ain't on my side at all.

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:26.731
I'm sorry I broke that lamp,
meemaw.

00:09:26.731 --> 00:09:30.302
But stop saying it was a relic
from the Ming Dynasty

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:33.838
because Ronald McDonald
was on that lamp.

00:09:33.838 --> 00:09:36.808
He wasn't around then.

00:09:36.808 --> 00:09:39.845
Donald Trump is not on the side
of people working really hard.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:42.180
He's on the side of people
working really hard for him,

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:45.618
and even then, he's not even on
their side enough to pay them.

00:09:45.618 --> 00:09:47.052
Rudy Giuliani
doesn't have enough money

00:09:47.052 --> 00:09:48.486
to cover his legal fees.

00:09:48.486 --> 00:09:50.756
And I bet he's still out there
trying to dig up dirt

00:09:50.756 --> 00:09:52.758
on Joe Biden
going country to country.

00:09:52.758 --> 00:09:55.393
"Boss, I mean, Chili, you'll
never believe what I found."

00:09:55.393 --> 00:09:57.629
"Sir, would you like
to order some appetizers?"

00:09:57.629 --> 00:10:01.167
"Oh, Rudy, you done it again."

00:10:01.167 --> 00:10:03.469
Liz Cheney is as responsible

00:10:03.469 --> 00:10:05.804
as anyone else in GOP leadership
for Trump's rise.

00:10:05.804 --> 00:10:09.241
This is not about heralding her
as a hero because she isn't one.

00:10:09.241 --> 00:10:12.077
It's about the GOP's hard
turn against democracy.

00:10:12.077 --> 00:10:15.247
She's being punished simply
for pointing out that Trump lost

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:17.516
and that his claim
that he won is a big lie.

00:10:17.516 --> 00:10:19.485
Republicans have made
the calculation

00:10:19.485 --> 00:10:21.486
that their party can't grow
without President Trump,

00:10:21.486 --> 00:10:22.788
even if democracy...

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:24.123
-Can't grow with
President Trump.

00:10:24.123 --> 00:10:26.726
-This has been A Closer Look.

